<tool id="yq" name="yq" version="@TOOL_VERSION@+galaxy@VERSION_SUFFIX@" profile="@PROFILE@">
    <description>Process YAML, JSON, XML, CSV, TSV, TOML and properties files</description>
    <macros>
        <import>macros.xml</import>
    </macros>
    <expand macro="requirements"/>
    <expand macro="version_command"/>
    <command detect_errors="aggressive"><![CDATA[
yq
#if $operation.mode == "eval-all":
  ea
#else:
  e
#end if
## Null-input mode for creating documents from scratch
#if $operation.mode == "create":
  -n
#end if
#if str($sec_format.input_format) != "auto":
  -p '$sec_format.input_format'
#end if
#if str($sec_format.output_format) != "auto":
  -o '$sec_format.output_format'
#end if
$sec_format.pretty_print:
-I $sec_format.indent
$sec_options.unwrap_scalar:
$sec_options.no_doc_separators
--security-disable-file-ops
--security-disable-env-ops
#if str($sec_options.front_matter) != "none":
  -f '$sec_options.front_matter'
#end if
## Expression: from file or inline text (written to configfile to avoid sanitization/escaping issues)
#if $expression_source.source == "file":
  --from-file '$expression_source.expression_file'
#else:
  --from-file '$expr_file'
#end if
## Input files
#if $operation.mode == "eval":
  '$operation.input_file'
#elif $operation.mode == "eval-all":
  #for $f in $operation.input_file:
    '$f'
  #end for
#end if
> '$output_file'
    ]]></command>
    <configfiles>
        <configfile name="expr_file">#if $expression_source.source == "text"
$expression_source.expression
#end if</configfile>
    </configfiles>
    <inputs>
        <conditional name="expression_source">
            <param name="source" type="select" label="Expression source" help="Choose whether to type the expression directly or load it from a file.">
                <option value="text" selected="true">Text input</option>
                <option value="file">From file</option>
            </param>
            <when value="text">
                <param name="expression" type="text" area="true" optional="false" label="Expression" help="The jq-like expression to evaluate (e.g. .a.b[0].c).">
                    <sanitizer sanitize="false"/>
                </param>
            </when>
            <when value="file">
                <param name="expression_file" type="data" format="txt" label="Expression file" help="A text file containing the jq-like expression to evaluate."/>
            </when>
        </conditional>
        <conditional name="operation">
            <param name="mode" type="select" label="Operation mode" help="eval processes a single input file; eval-all loads all documents from one or more files and runs the expression once on the combined set; create builds a new document from scratch without any input file.">
                <option value="eval" selected="true">Process a single input file</option>
                <option value="eval-all">Merge all documents (from one or more files)</option>
                <option value="create">Create a new document (no input)</option>
            </param>
            <when value="eval">
                <param name="input_file" type="data" format="yaml,json,xml,csv,tsv,txt" label="Input file" help="The data file to process."/>
            </when>
            <when value="eval-all">
                <param name="input_file" type="data" format="yaml,json,xml,csv,tsv,txt" multiple="true" label="Input file(s)" help="One or more data files. All documents from all files are loaded together."/>
            </when>
            <when value="create"/>
        </conditional>
        <section name="sec_format" expanded="true" title="Input/Output Format">
            <param name="input_format" type="select" label="Input format" help="Force the input format (default auto-detected from file extension).">
                <option value="auto" selected="true">auto</option>
                <option value="yaml">yaml</option>
                <option value="json">json</option>
                <option value="xml">xml</option>
                <option value="csv">csv</option>
                <option value="tsv">tsv</option>
                <option value="props">props</option>
                <option value="toml">toml</option>
                <option value="hcl">hcl</option>
                <option value="ini">ini</option>
                <option value="kyaml">kyaml</option>
                <option value="base64">base64</option>
                <option value="uri">uri</option>
                <option value="lua">lua</option>
            </param>
            <param name="output_format" type="select" label="Output format" help="Output format (default auto-determined from input).">
                <option value="auto" selected="true">auto</option>
                <option value="yaml">yaml</option>
                <option value="json">json</option>
                <option value="xml">xml</option>
                <option value="csv">csv</option>
                <option value="tsv">tsv</option>
                <option value="props">props</option>
                <option value="toml">toml</option>
                <option value="hcl">hcl</option>
                <option value="shell">shell</option>
                <option value="lua">lua</option>
                <option value="ini">ini</option>
            </param>
            <param name="pretty_print" type="boolean" checked="false" truevalue="-P" falsevalue="" label="Pretty print" help="Shorthand for pretty-printed output (indent style). Equivalent to ... style = ''"/>
            <param name="indent" type="integer" value="2" min="0" max="10" label="Indent level" help="Number of spaces for indentation in the output (default 2)."/>
        </section>
        <section name="sec_options" expanded="false" title="Advanced Options">
            <param name="unwrap_scalar" type="boolean" checked="true" truevalue="-r" falsevalue="-r=false" label="Unwrap scalars" help="Unwrap scalar values in the output (default true)."/>
            <param name="no_doc_separators" type="boolean" checked="false" truevalue="-N" falsevalue="" label="No document separators" help="Do not print --- document separators between YAML documents."/>
            <param name="front_matter" type="select" label="Front matter" help="Extract or process YAML front matter (e.g. in Markdown files).">
                <option value="none" selected="true">none</option>
                <option value="extract">extract</option>
                <option value="process">process</option>
            </param>
        </section>
    </inputs>
    <outputs>
        <data name="output_file" format="txt">
            <change_format>
                <when input="sec_format.output_format" value="yaml" format="yaml"/>
                <when input="sec_format.output_format" value="json" format="json"/>
                <when input="sec_format.output_format" value="xml" format="xml"/>
                <when input="sec_format.output_format" value="csv" format="csv"/>
                <when input="sec_format.output_format" value="tsv" format="tsv"/>
            </change_format>
        </data>
    </outputs>
    <tests>
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <conditional name="expression_source">
                <param name="source" value="file"/>
                <param name="expression_file" value="expr_read.txt" ftype="txt"/>
            </conditional>
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="mode" value="eval"/>
                <param name="input_file" value="simple.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="output_file" ftype="txt">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_line line="1"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <conditional name="expression_source">
                <param name="source" value="file"/>
                <param name="expression_file" value="expr_identity.txt" ftype="txt"/>
            </conditional>
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="mode" value="eval"/>
                <param name="input_file" value="simple.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            </conditional>
            <section name="sec_format">
                <param name="output_format" value="json"/>
            </section>
            <output name="output_file" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="&quot;a&quot;"/>
                    <has_text text="&quot;b&quot;"/>
                    <has_text text="1"/>
                    <has_text text="2"/>
                    <has_text text="3"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <conditional name="expression_source">
                <param name="source" value="file"/>
                <param name="expression_file" value="expr_identity.txt" ftype="txt"/>
            </conditional>
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="mode" value="eval"/>
                <param name="input_file" value="sample.json" ftype="json"/>
            </conditional>
            <section name="sec_format">
                <param name="output_format" value="yaml"/>
                <param name="pretty_print" value="true"/>
            </section>
            <output name="output_file" ftype="yaml">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="a:"/>
                    <has_text text="b:"/>
                    <has_text text="- 1"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <conditional name="expression_source">
                <param name="source" value="file"/>
                <param name="expression_file" value="expr_create.txt" ftype="txt"/>
            </conditional>
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="mode" value="create"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="output_file" ftype="txt">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="a:"/>
                    <has_text text="b:"/>
                    <has_text text="c: cat"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <conditional name="expression_source">
                <param name="source" value="file"/>
                <param name="expression_file" value="expr_merge.txt" ftype="txt"/>
            </conditional>
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="mode" value="eval-all"/>
                <param name="input_file" value="multi_doc.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="output_file" ftype="txt">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="a: 1"/>
                    <has_text text="b: 3"/>
                    <has_text text="c: 4"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <conditional name="expression_source">
                <param name="source" value="file"/>
                <param name="expression_file" value="expr_identity.txt" ftype="txt"/>
            </conditional>
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="mode" value="eval"/>
                <param name="input_file" value="simple.xml" ftype="xml"/>
            </conditional>
            <section name="sec_format">
                <param name="input_format" value="xml"/>
                <param name="output_format" value="yaml"/>
            </section>
            <output name="output_file" ftype="yaml">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="root:"/>
                    <has_text text="a:"/>
                    <has_text text="b:"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <conditional name="expression_source">
                <param name="source" value="file"/>
                <param name="expression_file" value="expr_merge.txt" ftype="txt"/>
            </conditional>
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="mode" value="eval-all"/>
                <param name="input_file" value="simple.yaml,simple2.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="output_file" ftype="txt">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="a:"/>
                    <has_text text="c: 3"/>
                    <has_text text="d: 4"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <conditional name="expression_source">
                <param name="source" value="text"/>
                <param name="expression" value=".a.b[0]"/>
            </conditional>
            <conditional name="operation">
                <param name="mode" value="eval"/>
                <param name="input_file" value="simple.yaml" ftype="yaml"/>
            </conditional>
            <output name="output_file" ftype="txt">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_line line="1"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
    </tests>
    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
**What it does**

`yq` is a lightweight and portable command-line YAML, JSON, XML, CSV, TSV, TOML, HCL, INI and properties processor. It uses `jq`-like syntax but works with many file formats.

**Usage**

Select an expression source (text input or file) and an operation mode:

- **Process a single input file** (`eval`): Evaluate the expression on a single input file. Each document in the file is processed in sequence.
- **Merge all documents** (`eval-all`): Load all documents from one or more input files and run the expression once on the combined set. Useful for merging multiple files or multi-document YAML.
- **Create a new document** (`create`): Build a new document from scratch without any input file. Null-input mode (`-n`) is automatically enabled.

`yq` will evaluate the expression and produce the output in the selected format.

-----

**Expression**

The expression uses `jq`-like syntax. Here are some quick examples:

- `.a.b[0].c` — navigate to `a`, then `b`, first element, then `c`
- `.items[].name` — select the `name` field of each item in the `items` array
- `.a.b.c = "value"` — set a value
- `. as $item ireduce ({}; . * $item)` — merge multiple documents

-----

**Examples**

- **Read a value**: Expression `.a.b[0]` on a YAML file returns the first element of `b` under `a`.
- **Convert YAML to JSON**: Set output format to `json`.
- **Convert JSON to YAML**: Set input format to `json` and output format to `yaml` with pretty print.
- **Create from scratch**: Select "Create a new document" mode and use expression `.a.b = "value"`.
- **Merge files**: Select "Merge all documents" mode with multiple files and expression `. as $item ireduce ({}; . * $item)`.

-----

**Security**

For safety in Galaxy, file operations (`load()`, `load_base64()`, etc.) and environment variable access (`env`) are always disabled and cannot be turned off by the user.

-----

**Documentation**

Full documentation: https://mikefarah.gitbook.io/yq/
    ]]></help>
    <expand macro="citations"/>
</tool>
